Author: {{ author_name }}, {{ author_role }}
Service: {{ service }}{% if specialist %} / Consulting: {{ specialist.department }} ({{ specialist.name }}){% endif %}
Patient: {{ patient_id }}
Admission Date: {{ admitted_at }}
Total Length of Stay: {{ los_days }} day(s)

PRINCIPAL DIAGNOSIS:
{{ primary_diagnosis }} ({{ primary_icd10 }}) — {{ severity | qualifier }} severity

SECONDARY DIAGNOSES:
{% if secondary_diagnoses %}
{% for dx in secondary_diagnoses %}
- {{ dx }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
- None identified during this admission
{% endif %}

HOSPITAL COURSE SUMMARY:
{{ hospital_course }}

PROCEDURES PERFORMED:
{% if procedures %}
{% for proc in procedures %}
- {{ proc }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
- No procedures performed
{% endif %}

SIGNIFICANT LABORATORY FINDINGS:
                    Admission        Discharge
  WBC:              {{ "%.1f"|format(cbc.wbc) }} 10³/µL        {{ "%.1f"|format(discharge_cbc.wbc) }} 10³/µL
  Creatinine:       {{ "%.2f"|format(bmp.creatinine) }} mg/dL         {{ "%.2f"|format(discharge_bmp.creatinine) }} mg/dL
  CRP:              {{ "%.1f"|format(inflammatory.crp) }} mg/L
{% if disease_specific.lactate is not none %}
  Peak Lactate: {{ "%.2f"|format(disease_specific.lactate) }} mmol/L
{% endif %}
{% if disease_specific.bnp is not none %}
  Peak BNP: {{ "%.0f"|format(disease_specific.bnp) }} pg/mL
{% endif %}
{% if disease_specific.glucose is not none %}
  Peak Glucose: {{ "%.1f"|format(disease_specific.glucose) }} mg/dL
{% endif %}

DISCHARGE CONDITION:
{% if severity == "mild" %}Stable — improved to baseline.
{% elif severity == "moderate" %}Stable — improved but close follow-up required.
{% elif severity == "severe" %}Guarded — significant residual deficits noted.
{% else %}Critical — transitioning to {{ discharge_disposition }}.{% endif %}

DISCHARGE DISPOSITION:
{{ discharge_disposition | upper }}

DISCHARGE MEDICATIONS:
{% for med in discharge_medications %}
- {{ med }}
{% endfor %}

FOLLOW-UP INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Follow up with primary care physician in {{ followup_days }} days.
{% if specialist_followup %}
2. {{ specialist_followup }} follow-up in 1–2 weeks.
{% endif %}
3. Return to ED immediately for worsening symptoms, fever > 38.5°C, or any new concerning symptoms.

PATIENT EDUCATION:
Patient and family educated on diagnosis, medications, activity restrictions, and return precautions. Verbalized understanding.

